Load decks of sp_resistor, sp_capacitor, sp_inductor against ngspice-45: one deck per (form, condition), written by
../load.py passive. Builds as in ../mos1/runs.out (devices/res, cap, ind; devices/spice/{resistor,capacitor,inductor}.va).
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh passive`. i(vd) in A for r_*, |i(vd)| at 1 MHz
for c_* and l_* (an inductor behind 1 ohm). nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of off (80 C, m=3); every deck gives tc1 and
tc2 (instance on the value forms, model on the geometry forms); geometry: rsh, narrow, short, l, w (r); cj, cjsw, narrow,
short, w, l (c); csect, length, mu, nt (l). Both simulators shorten and narrow a resistor by twice short and narrow
(r_geometry_nom: 100*(10u-0.4u)/(2u-0.2u) = 533.3 ohm). Result: no difference.

